{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/topij/agentic-dev-kit/issues/comments/5624454595","html_url":"https://github.com/topij/agentic-dev-kit/pull/731#issuecomment-5624454595","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/topij/agentic-dev-kit/issues/731","id":5624454595,"node_id":"IC_kwDOTNg3cs8AAAABTz5dww","user":{"login":"topij","id":5101841,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDE4NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5101841?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/topij","html_url":"https://github.com/topij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/topij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/topij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/topij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/topij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/topij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/topij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/topij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/topij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/topij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-10T19:43:15Z","updated_at":"2026-09-10T19:43:15Z","author_association":"OWNER","body":"Independent correctness review at `b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45` on 2026-09-10. This records the completed report before disposition or fixes; it is not a clean-review gate receipt. Actual runtime: `gpt-6-astra`, effort `high`.\n\nReviewed repository `topij/agentic-dev-kit`, handed path `/private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness/handed-tree`. `git rev-parse HEAD` actually returned `b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45`. I reviewed the named `f408039dc3a9b0d2e0e8d246c126af892839cee8...b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45` diff, not a moving HEAD. On 2026-09-10, `git diff --shortstat f408039dc3a9b0d2e0e8d246c126af892839cee8...b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45` in that tree printed `98 files changed, 61589 insertions(+), 45 deletions(-)`. The initial identity and command output are in [initial-identity.json](initial-identity.json).\n\n`git remote -v` identified `https://github.com/topij/agentic-dev-kit.git`. The wrapped `git ls-remote https://github.com/topij/agentic-dev-kit.git refs/heads/main` returned `f408039dc3a9b0d2e0e8d246c126af892839cee8` on 2026-09-10, establishing the supplied base against the remote: [remote-base-retry.log](remote-base-retry.log). The supplied branch name was not used as revision evidence.\n\nPrivate clone: `/private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness/mut-correctness-b018a054-x4aigsj1/repo`, created with `git clone --no-hardlinks` into a fresh correctness/revision namespace. All test and verification runs used the serial wrapper below, from that clone, with isolated state and caches. Clone creation, private mutation writes and wrapped verification were allowed. Default sandbox DNS blocked the initial remote lookup and `make test` dependency fetch; approved escalated retries succeeded in reaching those services. Default `ps` was refused; an approved read-only retry identified the occupied verification lock. No approval-review rejection occurred. No refused deletion, fetch into the handed tree, policy change, forge write, retained-tree write or additional agent was attempted.\n\n```sh\npython3 -B /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/review-state/serial-verify.py /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness/mut-correctness-b018a054-x4aigsj1/repo /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness -- <command and arguments>\n```\n\nP3 — focused guard tests do not pin the root-symlink exclusion. Coverage gap; no demonstrated production regression. At `scripts/conftest.py:237`, deleting `not state_dir.is_symlink() and` lets the new root-file branch hash a symlink target. The submitted `scripts/tests/test_state_guard.py` still passes under that mutation. The unchanged production guard deliberately leaves root symlinks outside this branch, and my independent target-content probe confirms that behavior. A negative behavioral case using a root symlink to a regular file would pin that compatibility boundary. This is a focused-suite survival, not a claim that the mutant survives the full repository suite. No other actionable correctness finding emerged from the changed guard, added test bodies, upgrade wording, changelog, handoff changes and execution records.\n\nVerification observations below are for `b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45` on 2026-09-10 in `/private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness/mut-correctness-b018a054-x4aigsj1/repo`, with deliberate guard overlays only where stated. Exact wrapper argv and full output are retained in the linked logs.\n\n- `python3 -B /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/review-state/serial-verify.py /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness/mut-correctness-b018a054-x4aigsj1/repo /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness -- make test`: initial sandbox attempt exited `2` during lint dependency fetching, before pytest ([make-test.log](make-test.log)). The approved retry reached the terminal summary: `1 failed, 2503 passed, 1 skipped in 381.11s (0:06:21)`, make exit `2` ([make-test-retry.log](make-test-retry.log)). The failure is `scripts/tests/test_pr_followup_hook.py::test_a_payload_too_deep_for_json_load_still_exits_zero`, matching the disclosed #393 failure. This is not a passing full-suite verdict.\n- `python3 -B /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/review-state/serial-verify.py /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness/mut-correctness-b018a054-x4aigsj1/repo /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness -- uv run --with pytest --with pyyaml python -B -m pytest scripts/tests/test_state_guard.py scripts/tests/test_kit_doctor.py::test_kit_repo_self_check_is_clean -q` after restoration: `54 passed in 12.56s`, exit `0`; includes the actual manifest self-check without drift deselection ([restored-state-guard.stdout.log](restored-state-guard.stdout.log), [command record](restored-state-guard.json)).\n- `python3 -B /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/review-state/serial-verify.py /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness/mut-correctness-b018a054-x4aigsj1/repo /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness -- python3 -B /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness/review-checks.py audit`: exit `0`. Checked the submitted execution SHA index, command stdout/stderr hashes, equality of retained checkpoint `trees`/`original_paths`, and changed manifest entries ([evidence-audit.log](evidence-audit.log)). This checks retained observations, not absence of transient historical writes.\n- `python3 -B /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/review-state/serial-verify.py /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness/mut-correctness-b018a054-x4aigsj1/repo /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness -- uv run --with pytest --with pyyaml python -B /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness/independent-probes.py`: exit `0`. In `scripts` and `scripts/devkit` layouts, synthetic nested pytest sessions detected empty-root-file creation, file deletion, file-to-directory replacement and directory-to-file replacement; their filesystem postconditions, failure exits and exact root-path diagnostics were asserted. A root symlink's target-content change stayed outside detection, as documented. Each synthetic cwd and subprocess argv is retained in [independent-probes.json](independent-probes.json), with full per-case stdout/stderr under this evidence directory.\n- `python3 -B /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/review-state/serial-verify.py /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness/mut-correctness-b018a054-x4aigsj1/repo /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness -- python3 -B /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness/final-attestation.py`: exit `0`. Separately executed `bash -n` for `scripts/dev_session.sh`, `scripts/reconcile_sessions.sh`, `scripts/lib/repo_root.sh`, `scripts/hooks/pre-push`, and `sh -n init.sh`. Each returned `0`. These are parse checks, not shell-behavior claims ([final-attestation.json](final-attestation.json)).\n\nMutation evidence: `python3 -B /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/review-state/serial-verify.py /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness/mut-correctness-b018a054-x4aigsj1/repo /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness -- python3 -B /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness/review-checks.py mutations` ran each case using `uv run --with pytest --with pyyaml python -B -m pytest scripts/tests/test_state_guard.py scripts/tests/test_kit_doctor.py::test_kit_repo_self_check_is_clean -q -m 'not driftcheck'`. Every run explicitly selected the manifest self-check before excluding its marker, and reported `1 deselected`. Original guard bytes were saved from `git show b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45:scripts/conftest.py`; the changed file was re-read and compared before testing. The diffs below change the intended branch. Every case restored the saved original bytes and verified equality before the next case.\n\n| Mutation | Actual behavioral result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Remove root-file branch | `4 failed, 49 passed, 1 deselected in 16.44s`, exit `1`; new/modified cases fail in flat/nested layouts because inner pytest incorrectly exits successfully | [diff](removed-root-file-branch.diff), [stdout](removed-root-file-branch.stdout.log), [command](removed-root-file-branch.json), [restoration](removed-root-file-branch-restoration.json) |\n| Replace root content hash with `\"<file>\"` | `2 failed, 51 passed, 1 deselected in 12.52s`, exit `1`; modified cases fail in flat/nested layouts | [diff](constant-root-file-hash.diff), [stdout](constant-root-file-hash.stdout.log), [command](constant-root-file-hash.json), [restoration](constant-root-file-hash-restoration.json) |\n| Remove root-symlink exclusion | `53 passed, 1 deselected in 12.56s`, exit `0`; survives focused suite | [diff](follow-root-file-symlink.diff), [stdout](follow-root-file-symlink.stdout.log), [command](follow-root-file-symlink.json), [restoration](follow-root-file-symlink-restoration.json) |\n\nThe failing mutation assertions check inner process exits after actual writes, not text/hash drift. Final restored guard SHA-256 is `a0a82682c9431205f8c0db80176694b37800da7964e5b77ec3eba283fc7569c2`, equal to the original reviewed bytes. [mutation-run.log](mutation-run.log) retains mutation diffs, results and restoration readbacks together.\n\nAttestation: I did not write the submitted code and used fresh context without another agent's findings. I followed Report, don't fix and No writes in the tree you were given. I did not repoint either handed HEAD or branch. On 2026-09-10 at `b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45`, the final wrapped `git --no-optional-locks -C /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness/handed-tree status --short` returned empty stdout, and `git --no-optional-locks -C /private/tmp/item5-b-kit-repair-1kc2i4t2/reviews/b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45/correctness/handed-tree diff --exit-code b018a0544c44028c21399ad073ce8a3dee3bfd45 --` returned empty stdout and exit `0`. The private clone gave the same status/diff observations. [Final attestation](final-attestation.json) records actual HEAD and command outputs. Status supports absence of tracked/untracked working-tree changes; it does not alone prove absence of a same-SHA detach or transient writes. No such repointing command was issued.\n\nEvery verification process started by this lens was polled to a terminal result. No verification command remains running or was cut off. The full suite failed as disclosed; the focused checks passed after restoration; the surviving mutation limits the coverage claim. No repair or merge authority is implied by this report.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/topij/agentic-dev-kit/issues/comments/5624454595/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"pin":null}